                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Welcome to the cesspool of Steam![/h1]\n\n[i]Telepathy Zero[/i] is a game that clearly took an hour to an afternoon to develop.  It's your typical \"Guess which of these 3 cards I'm thinking of\" game with very little thought and effort involved.  Of course, it's a title made in Unity, but it only feels like your basic test run as someone's very first project of being a developer.\n\nBoot up the game and get some ugly robot girl called \"Lisa\" who appears to tell you some message concluded with \"Click to Continue\", which throws you right into the \"game\".  This basically means there's a bug involving the introductory character not finishing her statement as the game just begins.\n\nAs I stated earlier, you're given 3 choices to choose from:  a red triangle, a green square, and a blue circle.  If you guess right, it starts to give you a win-streak.  If you guess wrong (which is quite likely), you'll lose your streak.  On the sides, you'll see image links to two of the dev's other games, which is aesthetically a good choice a developer could do, but a misclick could cause the game popus to be quite annoying.\n\nPersonally, I grabbed my trusty autoclicker and set it to the green square.  After that, I promptly flipped the game off and told it to play itself as I walked away.  When I came back after half an hour, I was fortunate enough to find myself at a 15 win-streak, thus 100%-ing [i]Telepathy Zero[/i].  This method also bugs the game out to the point of either showing the correct answer before asking \"Which am I thinking of?\" or even saying your guess is correct as it displays no color or shape (just its usual blank white screen).  During this experience, you can expect no sound effects  to alleviate the boredom, just a single song....\n\nI know for a short game, this has been a long read and I congratulate your effort and support in looking into my quality reviews!   That said, no...I didn't have fun with this basic guessing game.  It's good that it's free, but the idea is unoriginal and the game demands a minimum of a 10 win streak.  Only get it if you want a free game with achievements or if you enjoy leaving your autoclicker going while you're away from your computer.\n\n0/10  Zero like my \"telepathy\"...but my autoclicker's telepathy is INFINITE!!!",
